{
  "name": "Ricochet",
  "created": "2026-09-09T18:24:17.517Z",
  "notes": "Shapes launched from one end that bounce off the middle of the strip. There is no collision here and nothing in `SpawnerEmitter` knows what a wall is -- `mirror` folds the coordinate about its centre, so a shape crossing that point re-emerges travelling the other way. `MirrorWarp::toSource` is `|pos - centre| * 2`, which means the reflection is EXACT and free, and it costs one warp.\n\nThe mirror's `centre` is on a slow triangle, so the wall moves. A shape launched while the wall is far travels most of the strip before turning; one launched while it is near turns almost immediately. Same emitter, same velocity, completely different flight -- and because the wall keeps moving while a shape is in the air, the turn happens somewhere neither the launch nor the wall alone determines.\n\nThe chain is `M2 -> M0.rate`, the launch clock on a noise source, so shots arrive in bursts and gaps rather than on a beat. `colouring: \"speed\"` with `drag` 0.7 means each shape is born hot and cools as it slows, so you can read how long ago a thing was fired from its colour alone. Split complement: cerise and violet for the shapes with acid lime 200 degrees away on the wall glow, which is the only thing marking where the fold currently is.",
